        "original_id": "3194c9fb-42d1-5780-9dd0-81478be4f748",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: San Antonio, Texas; Yakutat, Alaska\n- Airports: San Antonio International Airport; Yakutat Airport; Yakutat Army Airfield\n- Companies: M7 Aerospace\n- Topics: airport identifiers; redevelopment\n\nFacts:\n- San Antonio International Airport is an international airport in San Antonio, Texas, that serves the Greater San Antonio metropolitan area.\n- San Antonio International Airport has the identifiers IATA SAT, ICAO KSAT, and FAA LID SAT.\n- M7 Aerospace LP is an aerospace company headquartered on the property of San Antonio International Airport in Uptown San Antonio, Texas.\n- Yakutat Army Airfield was redeveloped into Yakutat Airport after the airfield closed.\n- Yakutat Airport is a state-owned, public-use airport located three nautical miles southeast of the central business district of Yakutat, Alaska.\n- Yakutat Airport has the identifiers IATA YAK, ICAO PAYA, and FAA LID YAK.\n- Yakutat is a city and borough in Alaska that has no road access to the outside world.",
